HOW IT'S MADE
------------------------

- Install the Qt (Free Community edition)
  
  NOTE. During installation, select "Qt XX for desktop development" and "Custom Installation".
  In a tree, specify "Qt for Development > Qt > Qt XX > MSVC 2022 64-bit" (not just "MINGW", which can be unselected).

- In Visual Studio, install the "Qt Visual Studio Tools" extension.

  It will ask to configure the Qt version by selecting the folder with previously installed Qt (path to MSVC subfolder).
  Just press "Autodetect".

- In Visual Studio, load the "QtWorker.slnx" solution. If required, edit the code.

- Build the "Release", "x64" configuration. 

  If 'qtdeploy.targets(318,5): error MSB4023: Cannot evaluate the item metadata "%(Fullpath)"...' error appears, it can be ignored.

  It will generate the next files in "x64\Release":
    
    - "Qt6Core.dll"
    - "QtWorker.exe"

- Commit the "Qt6Core.dll" and "QtWorker.exe" files.

NOTE. The "QtWorker.vcxproj" project must not be added to main solution.